#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Mango Finder: the MangOS file manager, laid out like the Mac's Finder.

usage: mangos-finder [FOLDER or URI]     open a window
       mangos-finder --daemon            in the background (started at login)
       mangos-finder --preferences       Mango Finder Settings
       mangos-finder --connect           Connect to Server
       mangos-finder --select FILE       open its folder with it selected
       mangos-finder --info FILE         Get Info

  - sidebar: Favourites (Recents, Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Pictures,
    Music, Videos, Home), Locations (drives, USB sticks, phones, cameras,
    with an Eject button; Computer, Trash), Network (Network browsing,
    connected servers, Connect to Server)
  - views (Ctrl+1..4 like Cmd+1..4): Icons (thumbnails for photos, videos,
    PDFs through Tumbler); List (folders open in place with a triangle;
    Name, Date Modified, Size, Kind); Columns (each folder opens in a new
    column, the last one previews the selected file); Gallery (a large
    preview with a strip of thumbnails below)
  - sort by name, date, size or kind, ascending or descending, folders first
  - search in the folder, show hidden files (Ctrl+Shift+.)
  - back / forward (Ctrl+[ / Ctrl+]), enclosing folder (Ctrl+Up), open
    (double click, Enter, Ctrl+Down), Quick Look (Space), Copy Path,
    path bar at the bottom, new window (Ctrl+N), Home / Desktop / Documents
    (Ctrl+Shift+H / D / O), Network (Ctrl+Shift+K)
  - copy / cut / paste (Ctrl+C / X / V; Ctrl+Alt+V moves, like Cmd+Option+V),
    drag and drop (same disk: move, another disk or Ctrl: copy), Move to
    Trash (Delete or Ctrl+Backspace), Rename (F2), New Folder (Ctrl+Shift+N),
    New Document (empty, or from the Templates folder), Duplicate (Ctrl+D),
    Make Alias (Ctrl+L), Show Original (Ctrl+R), Compress (.zip, like the
    Mac), Extract Here, Undo (Ctrl+Z); in the Trash: Put Back, Delete
    Immediately, Empty Trash; progress bar with Stop; asks before replacing
    (mangos.fileops does the work and has its own tests)
  - Open With (the default app, the others, Other... with "always"), Get
    Info (Ctrl+I: kind, size, where, dates, Open With for all such files,
    permissions, a drive's capacity), Open in Terminal
  - drives: USB sticks, disks, phones and cameras open by themselves when
    connected and show a window (Settings: Ctrl+,); Eject (Ctrl+E)
  - network: Windows, Mac and NAS shares found on the network, Connect to
    Server (Ctrl+K: smb://, sftp://, ftp://, dav(s)://) with recent servers
  - for the desktop and the other apps it is the file manager (D-Bus
    org.freedesktop.FileManager1, org.xfce.FileManager, org.xfce.Trash):
    folders on the desktop, "Show in folder", the desktop's copy / move /
    Trash / rename go through it
Files go through GIO/GVFS, so drives, the Trash and network places behave
the same everywhere."""
